{title: Always With You}
{subtitle: Psalms 73:23–24}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
My [Bb]heart was filled with bitter pain
My in[Eb]most be[Gm]ing felt [F]the stain
I was sense[Eb]less and blind [Gm]of sight
A [F]brute beast in [Eb]the cold of [Gm]night
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Yet I am [F]always with you [Bb]
You hold me [Eb]by my right [Bb]hand
You guide me [Gm]with your counsel [F]true
And lift me [Eb]up when [F]I am un[Gm]done
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Afterward you [Eb]will take [F]me
Into the glo[Bb]ry you [Bb]decree
Whom have I in [Bb/D]heaven [Gm]but you?
With you [F]my soul has nothing [Eb]due
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Yet [Gm]I am [F]always with [Eb]you
You [Gm]hold me by [F]my right [Bb]hand
You guide me [Eb]with your counsel [Bb]true
And lift me [Gm]up when I am [F]undone
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
My flesh [Eb]and my [F]heart may [Gm]fail
But you [Eb]are the [F]rock of my [Bb]soul
My [Gm]portion for[F/A]ever [Bb]and [Gm]my goal
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]I am al[Eb]ways with you
[Gm]You [F]hold me by my right [Eb]hand
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
